  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is a large jump over singleprofile (0.653 vs 0.520), and transformer vs avgpool makes negligible difference (0.653 vs 0.650). Image alone is very weak (0.208). Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether scgpt, a different RNA foundation model encoder, could outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting. This experiment (config_009: rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is a clean single-variable change from our best result, isolating the encoder effect. It is the best use of this slot because: (1) if scgpt improves over scvi_n200, we identify a stronger backbone to build multimodal models on in the remaining 4 experiments; (2) if it does not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can confidently allocate remaining budget to multimodal fusion experiments with the known-best encoder. This reduces the most important remaining uncertainty (encoder choice) before committing budget to more complex multimodal configurations."
